What are you playing?

00:15:53.980 --> 00:15:54.900
Did you just get it?

00:15:54.980 --> 00:15:56.440
So, you're probably playing Breath of the Wild.

00:15:56.760 --> 00:16:01.200
Or, did you just get it and you're playing Kirby Star Allies and you're like, this is the Switch?

00:16:01.380 --> 00:16:03.020
This is what they have?

00:16:03.020 --> 00:16:04.480
And you're like, no, dude.

00:16:04.620 --> 00:16:05.780
Like, come on. Play Odyssey.

00:16:06.120 --> 00:16:07.260
Play Breath of the Wild.

00:16:07.280 --> 00:16:11.620
But then you have this other friend over here saying like, no, play Donkey Kong 3.

00:16:11.960 --> 00:16:14.980
And you leave that friend forever.

00:16:15.180 --> 00:16:26.440
Okay? You don't speak another word to them because chances are if they make statements like that, if they're just willing to recommend Donkey Kong 3, they're also likely to recommend things that could kill you.

00:16:28.060 --> 00:16:33.520
So, with that piece of foreshadowing, Mike, what are your thoughts on the Essential Games list?

00:16:33.540 --> 00:16:34.420
I'm so glad you asked.

00:16:34.520 --> 00:16:40.700
Unfortunately, first, I'm going to read Joe's thoughts because I didn't even read Joe's thoughts for Donkey Kong 3 ahead of time.

00:16:40.840 --> 00:16:42.780
I needed to be surprised by something.

00:16:43.260 --> 00:16:45.980
So, here are Joe's thoughts on Donkey Kong 3.

00:16:45.980 --> 00:16:48.240
If you don't know who Joe is, if you're just like, who's Joe?

00:16:48.400 --> 00:16:49.280
Why are we reading his thoughts?

00:16:49.520 --> 00:16:51.460
He is on this show occasionally.

00:16:51.620 --> 00:16:53.480
He's a good guy. He has fun thoughts.

00:16:53.640 --> 00:16:54.980
He worships Duck Hunt.

00:16:56.500 --> 00:17:02.140
So, Donkey Kong 3 is very different from the last two games, Joe says, concerned.

00:17:02.760 --> 00:17:07.900
It is more action-based, but overall, it's still not a long game and doesn't have a ton of depth.

00:17:08.180 --> 00:17:19.040
Just like the other DK games so far, I can see it being fun today as the kind of game you play on your phone while you're waiting for a train or something, but it can get old fast.

00:17:19.780 --> 00:17:22.300
Especially if you are not nostalgic for it.

00:17:22.520 --> 00:17:25.480
Not essential. It seems like Joe maybe liked it.

00:17:25.820 --> 00:17:31.060
I don't know. I mean, yeah. I think he seems to give these games the benefit of the doubt more often than not.

00:17:31.060 --> 00:17:33.300
He gave it the BOTD? Yeah, that one.

00:17:33.300 --> 00:17:34.420
The benefit of the doubt.

00:17:34.620 --> 00:17:35.700
That's true. The BOTD.

00:17:35.800 --> 00:17:40.560
That's the acronym. But if you want to know how I feel about this game, I don't really know how to...

00:17:40.560 --> 00:17:43.540
I want to do something for the fans of this game, right?

00:17:44.580 --> 00:17:45.800
It's not essential, okay?

00:17:46.040 --> 00:17:47.740
But you want to know why.

00:17:47.820 --> 00:17:50.040
And it can't be that I don't like the game, because I agree.

00:17:50.040 --> 00:17:51.180
That's not a good reason.

00:17:52.440 --> 00:17:58.680
The reason why I think this game is not essential is because it has no Nintendo vibe on it, first off.

00:17:58.840 --> 00:18:00.560
It doesn't have any of their, like...

00:18:00.560 --> 00:18:03.420
Any of the love that they put into Donkey Kong 1 and Donkey Kong Jr.

00:18:03.440 --> 00:18:04.880
is not there in 3.

00:18:04.880 --> 00:18:14.380
The addition of this random Stanley dude, the only thing that's amazing about Stanley is that he also shows up in the Saturday Supercade episode about Donkey Kong 3.

00:18:14.560 --> 00:18:18.820
No way. Yeah. Saturday Supercade with Donkey Kong and Donkey Kong Jr.

00:18:19.000 --> 00:18:23.560
In one of the Donkey Kong episodes, it's called Greenhouse Gorilla.

00:18:23.860 --> 00:18:26.500
And it shows Donkey Kong messing with Stanley.

00:18:26.740 --> 00:18:28.640
Jeez. We can't escape cartoons.

00:18:28.820 --> 00:18:32.680
We can't escape random references in these shows, even in our essential games list.

00:18:33.500 --> 00:18:38.260
And Stanley, being in this game, shows that Nintendo just kind of threw this thing together.

00:18:38.480 --> 00:18:42.080
The concept of this being another Donkey Kong game is laughable.

00:18:42.400 --> 00:18:44.380
Throwing the 3 on there is weird.

00:18:44.380 --> 00:18:49.960
Weird. But also, like we talked about very early in this and just kind of said one and done with it on the gameplay.

00:18:50.200 --> 00:18:52.040
It's a mess. There's too much going on.

00:18:52.480 --> 00:18:53.720
Too much to focus on.

00:18:53.840 --> 00:18:56.440
And it's not necessarily rewarding to the player.

00:18:56.740 --> 00:19:02.300
No. I imagine there is a strategy to be good at it, but I can't imagine that being all that fun.

00:19:02.560 --> 00:19:03.820
Not essential. Sean?

00:19:04.040 --> 00:19:07.860
I think this was back when they were primarily...

00:19:09.740 --> 00:19:11.820
Nintendo has a reputation now.

00:19:12.800 --> 00:19:22.380
They have faltered on it in the past, and they have gained and lost goodwill with their followers over the years.

00:19:22.580 --> 00:19:24.580
But I think this was before that...

00:19:24.580 --> 00:19:28.220
This was definitely before that was even like a trope for them.

00:19:28.540 --> 00:19:33.560
They were just trying to make money, and they still needed to...

00:19:33.560 --> 00:19:40.000
I still liked that they wanted to try new things, but this was too much of a departure,

00:19:40.000 --> 00:19:41.940
and it seemed like a cop-out.

00:19:42.420 --> 00:19:48.260
Yeah. I'm still not entirely sure.

00:19:48.380 --> 00:19:54.000
I would have loved to get some kind of developer interview or something, or just like some traces of something.

00:19:54.100 --> 00:19:59.560
Yeah. But we don't have it, and so we'll never really know the full story behind Donkey Kong 3.

00:19:59.780 --> 00:20:03.520
I do know that the gaming historian on YouTube, he's a great guy,

00:20:04.020 --> 00:20:08.520
he has like a Donkey Kong 3 video, just kind of on the history of it,

00:20:08.800 --> 00:20:10.560
but I don't know how much he goes into it.

00:20:10.640 --> 00:20:13.880
